lesson: 85
title: How many groups
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes we know how many go in each group and must find how many groups we can make.
explain: Divide the total by the size of one group.
explain: 30 pencils in packs of 5 make 30 ÷ 5 = 6 packs.
vars: a=name t=thing e=2..10 g=2..10
let: n = g * e
answer: n / e
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}. {a.He} puts {e} {t} in each bag. How many bags does {a} fill?
exercise: There are {n} {t}. Each box holds {e} {t}. How many boxes are needed?
exercise: {a} makes piles of {e} {t} from {n} {t}. How many piles does {a} make?
exercise: {n} children stand in teams of {e}. How many teams are there?
exercise: {a} gives {e} {t} to each friend and gives away {n} {t} in all. How many friends get {t}?
test: How many packs of {e} can be made from {n} {t}?
test: A baker puts {e} rolls on each tray and bakes {n} rolls. How many trays does the baker use?
test: {n} {t} are packed in bags, {e} {t} to a bag. How many bags are there?
test: {a} wants every jar to hold {e} {t}. {a.He} has {n} {t}. How many jars will {a.he} fill?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t} and puts them in bags of {e}. How many bags does {a} use?
