exercise: {n} {t} are packed {e} per bag. How many bags are filled?
exercise: A farmer in Devon puts {e} eggs in each carton and has {n} eggs. How many cartons does he fill?
exercise: {a} gives {e} {t} apiece to some friends and hands out {n} {t} altogether. How many friends got {t}?
exercise: A shelf in a library in Toronto holds {e} books, and there are {n} books. How many shelves do the books fill?
test: Into how many groups of {e} can {n} {t} be split?
test: Every car in a parade in Sydney carries {e} children. {n} children ride in the parade. How many cars are there?
test: With {n} {t} and {e} {t} in every packet, how many packets does {a} make?
test: {a} puts {e} stickers on each card and uses {n} stickers in all. How many cards does {a.he} make?
test: A school in Dublin takes {n} pupils on a trip, {e} pupils in each group. How many groups are there?
