exam: A quantity of {n} {t} is packed into bags, each bag containing precisely {e} {t}. Determine the number of bags so filled.
exam: It is given that each receptacle accommodates {e.words} {t}. Ascertain the number of receptacles required to contain {n.words} {t}, all receptacles being filled.
exam: Compute the number of groups of {e} contained in {n}.
exam: State the number of complete sets which {a} may form from {n} {t}, each set consisting of {e} {t}, no item remaining.
exercise: Since Dad was laid off, he pays back the {n} dollars he owes at {e} dollars a week. How many weeks will it take?
